
# ==========================================
# Agasobanuye Fast - Git Ignore
# ==========================================

# Node.js dependencies
node_modules/
backend/node_modules/
frontend/node_modules/

# Environment files and secrets
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.production.example

# Private application data
backend/database.json

# SQLite databases and temporary files
*.db
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.sqlite-journal

# Uploaded movies, images, and user files
uploads/
backend/uploads/
frontend/uploads/
storage/
backend/storage/

# Logs
*.log
logs/
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
pnpm-debug.log*

# Build and coverage output
dist/
build/
coverage/
.tmp/
temp/
.cache/

# Editor and IDE settings
.vscode/
.idea/
*.suo
*.user
*.code-workspace

# Operating system files
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini

# Temporary and backup files
*.tmp
*.bak
*.old
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# Local development files
.local/
```
<text weight="semibold">Next, save the file in VS Code.</text>

Then open Command Prompt and run:

```cmd
cd /d "E:\project in vs code\Agasobanuye fast"

git rm -r -f --cached .vscode backend/database.json

git add .gitignore

git add .

git status
```

<box border={{size:1,color:"#16a34a"}} radius="lg" padding={3} gap={1}>
  **Important:** This keeps `.vscode` and `backend/database.json` out of the Git index, but does not delete your local copies. If your backend requires `backend/database.json` to start, we'll need to provide a safe replacement or initialization step for deployment.
</box>

Send me the output of `git status` before committing, so we can check that private files and uploaded movies are not included.